      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-10-26_WidnesExaminer_art0003" n="art0003">
        <p>LIONEL FAIRCLOUGH, Hon. Sec.</p>
        <p>(19th October, 1912). Investing Rural District Council with Urban Powers: Deternilning Speolal Expenses. • RUNCORN RURAL DISTRICT. —GRAPPEN- HALL CONTRIBUTORY PLACE. TO ' THE RURAL DISTRICT COUNCIL OF RUNCORN ; And .to all others to whom it may concern. WE, THE LOCAL GOVERNMENT BOARD, baying received and duly considered an application under Section 4of the Private Street Works Act, 1892, from the Rural District Council of Runcorn for the issue of an Order patting in force in the contributory place of Orappenhall, in their District, so far aa regards certain streets, certain provisions of that Act as herein-after mentioned, do hereby Declare and Order as follows : ARTICLE I.—Until We by Order otherwise direct, the provisions of the Private Street Works Act, 1892, except so far as they relate to the sewering of streets, shall be in force in the said contributory place, so ferns regards the streets herein-after described ; and the said Rural District Council shall, except as aforesaid, be invested with all the powers, rights, duties, capacities, liabili- ties, and obligations which an Urban District Council csaonitdriAbuotto, ryaoposu,ticree; sounder may, by the adoptionthoefsatihde streets ; that is to athaorseegparrodavitsrbi said do Victoria Avenue, throughout its existing extent as measured in a southerly direction from its junction with the Puirdio Highway leading to linutsford to a point 540 feet from the said junction. Albert Road, throughout its existing extent as measured in a southerly direction from its junction with the said Public Highway to a point 405 feet from the said junction. York Drive, throughout its existing extent as measured in an easterly direction from its junction with Victoria Road to a point distant 265 feet from the said junction, and thereafter (1) in a northerly direction for a further distance of 115 feet, and (2) in a southerly direction for a further distance of 235 feet.</p>
        <p>- - ARTICLE IL—The expenses incurred or payable by the said Rural District Council in the execution of the powers conferred upon them by Article I. of this Order, except so far as those expenses may relate to their Establishment and Officers shall be Special Expenses within the meaning of the Public Health Act, 1875, chargeable upon the said contributory place. ARTICLE M.—This Order shall come into operation on the Eleventh day of November, One thousand nine hundred and twelve, and the said Rural District Council shall cause it to be published once in some newspaper circulated within their District before that date. Given under the Seal of Office of the Local Government Board, this Nine- teenth day of October, in the year One Thousand nine hundred and twOve JOHN BURNS,' _ President.</p>
      </div>
