      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-10-26_WidnesExaminer_art0039" n="art0039">
        <head>RYLANDS' RECREATION v. SALFORD ST. BARTHOLOMEW'S.</head>
        <p>RYLANDS' RECREATION v. SALFORD ST. BARTHOLOMEW'S.</p>
        <p>The Warrington team carried all before them on the Gorsey-lane enclosure on Saturday, and piled on the phenomenal score of 8 goals 22 tries (82 points) to nil. The chief scorers were Hennessey one goal eight tries, Griffiths six tries, Morris three goals and two tries, Leah one goal and two tries, Booth one goal, Stretford two tries, Broadhurst and Horrocks one try each. RYLANDS TtECS V CLIFTON.-At Gorsey-lane. Teams: Full back, 0A Brarnhall ; three-quarter backe, T Hennessey, F Potter, A Horrocks, J Griffithg ; half backs, G Floyd, H Morris ; forwards, A Stretford, A Booth, F Mason, J Brandwooe, .1 Broadhurst, W Langley. Reserves, Barton and Welsby. Kick-off 3.30.</p>
        <p>TEAMS TO-DAY.</p>
        <p>EMMANUEL INSTITUTE V WALKER'S BREWERY.— At Arpley. Start 3 p.m. Team :—F Knight, goal ; G Lloyd, S Hughes, full backs ; S Fairhurst, P Hughes (capt), W Ares, half backs; E Ashpey, H Mather, W Newton, P Hamilton, S Banner, forwards.</p>
        <p>ADULT SCHOOL V DITTOS ST MARY'S.— At Ditton.— Adult School. P Beddard, goal ; F Wareing, G Bailey, full backs ; S Leigl., A Webb, fi Mather, half backs ; W Stewart, T Jackson, J Hamblett, W Dykee, LI Rowe, forwards.</p>
        <p>BANK QUAY RECS. v. WESToN POINT.—At Runcorn. Goal, W Bushell; R Spencer, G Redford; W Appleton. T Worrall, A Keenan; .1 Long, E Hughes, E Myles, A N Other, P Long; reserve, R Butler. 'Bus leaves 1.15 prompt. "</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-10-26_WidnesExaminer_art0040" n="art0040">
        <head>ASsOCIATION FOOTBALL.</head>
        <p>ASsOCIATION FOOTBALL.</p>
        <p>NORTH CHESHIRE LEAGUE. FIRST DI VISION.</p>
        <p>Goals. P. W. L. D. For Ag'st Pts Barnton Villa Broadheath Islobberley 9 0 0. 0 7. 1 4 Lostock Gralam Oughtriogton Park 3... 1... 1... 1... 2... 2... 3 Lyrom 3 1.. 1. ) 6. 7... 3 Latchford Bowdon Vale Altrincham Lads 4 0. " 9 5 8 . 9 OughtringtonAmat 2... 0... 2... 0... 4... 12... 0 St' Vincents</p>
        <p>Sr. VINCENT'S V BRoADHEATIT. At Stamford Park, before a fair attendance. Final: Broadbeath 4 goals, St. Vincents 1 goal. LYMM V MOBBF.RLEY. At Lymm. Lymm were without three of their usual players, Haddon, goal, being the most notably absentee, whilst Mobberley were practically at full strength. Shakeshaft making his first appearance. At the end of five minutes, Bayley got in a nice centre for Kempt to open the score for Mobberley. Give and take play followed for a time. After several futile attempts the home team were rewarded, Barber equalizing from a centre by Owen. Broom next gave Mobberley the lead. Aroused by this second reverse, Lymm attacked strongly and were awarded a penalty. Owen took the kick but Eden brought off a Eine save, whilst before the interval T Smith added point No. three for Mobberley. Half- time: Mobberley 3 goals, Lymm 1 goal. In the second half Cragg placed the issue beyond doubt by scoring another point f9r Mobberley. No further scoring took place. 1, inal : Mobberley 4 goals, Lymm I goal. SECOND DIVISION.</p>
        <p>Goals. P. W. L. D. for agst, Pts Weaver Refining Co 5... 2... 1... 2 4... 6... 6 Stockton Heath Latchford Britannia 4... 2... 2... 0_ 7_ 9... 4 Latchford Reserve '2... 1... 0... 1... G... 0... 3 Newton Common A 3... 1... 1... 1... 8... 6—• 3 Latchford Reos Padgate Amateurs Oughtrington Arrant 1... 1... 0... 0_ 5... 0... 2 Cadishead Wesleyan 3... 0... 1_ 2... 1... 5... 2 Warrington CL B 1... 0... 1... 0... o._ 4... 0</p>
        <p>•• --•• LATCHFORD BRITTANNIA V WARRINGTON C.L.B. The visitors winning the toss took advantage of the breeze hich was blowing from goal to goal. The Brigade goal had a narrow escape on two occasions, the ball being driven against the crossbar with Calderhank beaten. Just before the interval the Britannia took a well-deserved lead by opening the score. Playing with the wind, the Brittannia bad the major portion of the play and quickly added to their score. The Brigade made occasional excursions into the home quarters but met a sound defence. Cartwright in particular being noticeable, still holding the upper hand the soap makers added two further points end ran out winners with the score :—Latchford Brittannia, four goals ; Warrington C.L.8., STOCKTGN.HFATH V. WEAVER REFINING COMPANY. This game, which was postponed from the Saturday previous owing to the former being engaged in the re-played Cbetahire Cup Tie rook place at Stockton Heath on Saturday. Taken all through, the contest was of an even nature, and ended in a goalless draw. The Refiners threw away a splendid chance of victory. They were awarded a penalty, hot for encroaohing, the kick had to be taken again. This .time Isherwood brought off a magnificent save, and gave his side a somewhat lucky point. BATON VILLA V. ALTRINCHAM LADS. At Barnton. Reault : Barnton Villa, three ; Aftrincham Lads, one.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-10-26_WidnesExaminer_art0041" n="art0041">
        <head>WIDNES ALLIANCE LEAGUE.</head>
        <p>WIDNES ALLIANCE LEAGUE.</p>
        <p>GREAT SANKEY V. FARNWORTTI WESLEY GUILD. Played on the ground of the former Final : Great Sankey. 17 goals ; Farnworth Wesley Guild nil.</p>
        <p>FRIENDLY MATCHES.</p>
        <p>_ WAR To ADULT` ECLIOOL- v. EMMANUEL TNSTI- TUTE.—PIayed on Saturday, the Adult School winning by 2 goals to 1. 1</p>
