        <head>Hassail—Davies.</head>
        <p>Hassail—Davies.</p>
        <p>A very pretty wedding took place at St. fli3len's Church,Hollinfare. on Thursday, when Mr Sam Hassalt, son of Mrs Hassan,* Theolis-street, Warrington, was married to Miss Lucy Davies. daughter of the late It James. Davies,, of Elmhurst, Roll Mare Both the bride. and.bridegroom are particularly well known'.inlocar musical circles, Miss Davies being a popular vocalist,' while Mr Hassall is the conductor of the WArrington Male Choral Union The Vicar (Rev A F Whiter officiated. Mr W H Payton, Mus Bee., was at the: organ and played the f. 'Bowing selection ni ini his usual tasteful manner :—" Sault d'Ambnel (Elgar), "Romance. Sans . Paroles," "The "iThe Question " (IV olat•nhelnic), " clhant Sails P`ernles " (rachnikowaky), " Serenade '!„ (IF idor ). The bride who was given away by Net Niother .(3.1r ;James Davies,) was charmingly Attired in 'white aattin;and ninon. She wak attended Miss Mildred Davies, and Mikatiliiin Whiteeide:of Blackpool. Miss Davies wore a pretty dress of blue ninon over pink stbf; while Miss Whiteside 'was tsetefully gowned in pale ',lemon inon, over lemon- sati D. Both wOre caps Mf net, with •ftoWers'and vebiet riftb'm-:—.2MeGeorge Gibboons, of TkilAnclater, discitsiged chtlies of best man. The:reception was held at Elmhurst and later b4pry .5.„1.e,, Who were the reciplents of many atidsome pt:etienti, left ,for Bournemouth where the honeytncion- la being spent. Sherburn—England.</p>
