        <p>. . !•••1,.1 • .</p>
        <p>.</p>
        <p>Deep regret was occasioned in Warrington on • Scittlay ne4a 'that Mr. Edwin James Guest,•-' If'.A2,lP-1.• of the flittr'of ' Guest Bros.,' Ltd., tanners,l Winyrick-street,liad'';p4Med away ftarne,at 890ElenlYt at èHf ck 4' previous ey,ennig In.leancbestet/5 licAT)44l#l4esce,:,Clf,lilst old friend the Restr E.kAlt,yd •Jonaa,t,'a:,,proininent;Wesleyan minister wbbistiss! at , onaltimb fats tionedat Warrington: ' Mr Giatitt,*bo' was ' governor of i-Ryllitilfcßint Bt-hool;,-001 voyn Bay,'and he 'visited Manalegter,on Ft iday for the purpot.e of attending a meeting of the governor, ; 'which was to he 13841 in the ;afternoon. Towards noon, however, he was 'taken suddenly ill, and medical assistance was summoned.' For ,s short time be seemed to recover, bit there watt aOhnage for the worse, and he passed away at the time stated, The pause of. dead] keting.heant failure. Mr. Guest, who was one of the mot respected figures in the publitto life of Waridigiou, leaves a widow and two sons and</p>
